From: dnf-plugin-p2p contributors <none@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PeerStoreError crash in maybe_delete_peer_record

When the peerstore's garbage collection runs via maybe_delete_peer_record(),
calling self.addrs(peer_id) can raise PeerStoreError if the peer's data
has already expired or been removed from peer_data_map. The unhandled
exception crashes the entire libp2p event loop and kills the proxy daemon.

This patch wraps the addrs() call in a try/except for PeerStoreError.
If the error is raised, the peer record is removed since the peer has
no valid addresses anyway.

Upstream bug: https://github.com/libp2p/py-libp2p/issues/XXXX

---
 libp2p/peer/peerstore.py | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libp2p/peer/peerstore.py b/libp2p/peer/peerstore.py
index 54602937..d26a70fb 100644
--- a/libp2p/peer/peerstore.py
+++ b/libp2p/peer/peerstore.py
@@ -335,7 +335,11 @@ class PeerStore(IPeerStore):
         :param peer_id: The peer whose record we may delete/
         """
         if peer_id in self.peer_record_map:
-            if not self.addrs(peer_id):
+            try:
+                if not self.addrs(peer_id):
+                    self.peer_record_map.pop(peer_id, None)
+            except PeerStoreError:
+                # If the peer ID is expired or not found, it has no valid addresses, so remove its record.
                 self.peer_record_map.pop(peer_id, None)
 
     def consume_peer_record(self, envelope: Envelope, ttl: int) -> bool:
-- 
